    "sidebar": {
      "textColor": "#044f1c",
      "backgroundColor": "#c5f5a6",
      "selectors": [],
      "type": "sidebar",
      "description": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">To continue addressing the historical legacy of disparities in how communities of color and low-income populations have been affected by government actions, including transportation planning decisions, the MRMPO is committed to:</span></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Provide meaningful opportunities for public engagement with members of low-income and minority populations during the planning and development of programs, policies, and activities (including identification of potential effects, alternatives, and mitigation measures).</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">​Provide access to public information concerning the human health or environmental impacts of programs, policies, and activities on low-income and minority populations.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">Include explicit consideration of the effects of potential future regional transportation system planning scenarios on low-income and minority populations.</span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif\">In this map, the census tracts which make up the Albuquerque Metro Planning Area are colorized and highlighted to identify where racial and ethnic minorities and low-income population residents are most concentrated within the region in order to help assess the distribution of benefits and burdens of transportation planning decisions.</span></span></span></p>\n"
    },
